This VERSION file is the authoritative build identifier.
All visible labels, launcher, and window titles must match this version.

v2.0.0 rebuilt the Baccarat module as a local Python server application, replacing a five-file
browser prototype that was reviewed and found not releasable.

v2.1.0 added a Tie bet alongside Banker or Player, moved the disclaimer to the foot of the window and
removed page scrolling. v2.2.x put the panels beside the betting column for half-screen use, gave the
bead plate a fixed 10 x 10 box of small colour-only hands and renamed the panels. v2.3.0 made PASS
record the table's result. v2.4.0 gave the Tie insurance its own stake.

v2.5.0 added the OCR spot-check tool, an accuracy readout built from the audit log and a working
Gemini model id (gemini-3.8-flash). v2.5.1 proved the reading prompt against synthetic displays and
made that check gradable. v2.5.2 added a "Save a screenshot sample" button so a capture region can be
judged without a terminal.

v2.6.0 is where the reader met the real table: all four of the user's real screenshots read correctly,
and the exercise exposed three defects synthetic images had hidden — truncated replies discarded as
unparseable, a reasoning model returning nothing on a cluttered image, and empty replies not retried.
It also uncovered a private file accidentally synced to the public repository, which was removed and
now cannot happen again (the sync refuses images).

IMPORTANT: the capture region has not been calibrated (all 9 profiles are "calibrated": false), so the
module is not yet reading the live screen end to end. Gemini returns HTTP 503 for this key.

The per-release record for the module is BACARAT/CHANGELOG.md.
